1
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:24,000
No Job's too big, no Pup's too small.

2
00:08:36,000 --> 00:08:42,000
PAW Patrol: The Movie is a family, comedy,
adventure film directed by Cal Brunker.

3
00:12:54,000 --> 00:13:00,000
Ryder and the pups are called to Adventure City to stop Mayor Humdinger
from turning the bustling metropolis into a state of chaos.

4
00:17:12,000 --> 00:17:18,000
Gus (voice), played by Tyler Perry.

5
00:21:30,000 --> 00:21:36,000
Humdinger / Turbot (voice), played by Ron Pardo.

6
00:25:48,000 --> 00:25:54,000
Ryder (voice), played by Will Brisbin.

7
00:30:06,000 --> 00:30:12,000
Marshall (Voice), played by Kingsley Marshall.

8
00:34:24,000 --> 00:34:30,000
Rubble (voice), played by Keegan Hedley.

9
00:38:42,000 --> 00:38:48,000
Chase (voice), played by Iain Armitage.

10
00:43:00,000 --> 00:43:06,000
Paw Patrol: The Dino Movie is an upcoming Canadian animated action-adventure comedy
film based on the television series Paw Patrol created by Keith Chapman.

11
00:47:18,000 --> 00:47:24,000
Produced by Spin Master Entertainment, it is the sequel to Paw Patrol: The Movie (2021) and Paw Patrol: The Mighty
Movie (2023) and is being directed by Cal Brunker, who co-wrote the screenplay with Bob Barlen.

12
00:51:36,000 --> 00:51:42,000
The ensemble voice cast includes Mckenna Grace (voicing Skye), Jennifer Hudson, Fortune Feimster,
Snoop Dogg, Bill Nye, Meredith MacNeill, Paris Hilton, Terry Crews, and Jameela Jamil.

13
00:55:54,000 --> 00:56:00,000
In September 2023, before the release of Paw Patrol: The Mighty Movie, Spin Master announced
a third Paw Patrol film is in development with a planned 2026 release date.

14
01:00:12,000 --> 01:00:18,000
Returning crew members were announced soon after, including Brunker as a director
and Jennifer Dodge, Laura Clunie, and Toni Stevens as producers.

15
01:04:30,000 --> 01:04:36,000
Mikros Image in Montreal, like its predecessors, returned to handle the animation, this time collaborating
in Paris, with the casting of Grace, Hudson and Feimster being announced the following year.

16
01:08:48,000 --> 01:08:54,000
The film is based on the Dino Rescue sub-theme of the main show.

17
01:13:06,000 --> 01:13:12,000
Paw Patrol: The Dino Movie is scheduled to be released in Canada by Elevation
Pictures and the United States by Paramount Pictures on August 14, 2026.

18
01:17:24,000 --> 01:17:30,000
The film explores themes of cartoon, rescue mission, dog, animals, cartoon dog.

19
01:21:42,000 --> 01:21:48,000
The tone is lighthearted.
